('127.491.d.2.A',3,'The American Association for Respiratory Care publishes clinical practice guidelines that help therapists apply the best:','["standards of practice", "fashion", "menus", "movies"]'::jsonb,0,'Guidelines guide care.','original'),
('127.491.d.2.A',4,'Evidence-based guidelines for ventilator weaning are updated as new research becomes available, so therapists must stay:','["silent", "current", "unaware", "absent"]'::jsonb,1,'Update practice.','original'),
('127.491.d.2.B',3,'A patient on airborne precautions should be cared for in a room with negative:','["price", "music", "pressure", "color"]'::jsonb,2,'Negative pressure room.','original'),
('127.491.d.2.B',4,'Before entering a droplet-isolation room, a therapist should wear a surgical:','["hat only", "earring", "scarf", "mask"]'::jsonb,3,'Droplet precautions.','original'),
('127.491.d.2.C',3,'When moving a patient who is on a ventilator, the therapist protects the airway and uses proper body:','["mechanics", "music", "budget", "colors"]'::jsonb,0,'Safe transfers.','original'),
('127.491.d.2.C',4,'Securing ventilator tubing so it is not pulled when the patient is turned helps prevent accidental:','["intubation", "extubation", "vaccination", "hydration"]'::jsonb,1,'Prevent tube dislodgement.','original'),
('127.491.d.3.A',3,'Automatic breathing changes in response to carbon dioxide are regulated mainly by the brainstem and the branch that works without conscious thought, the autonomic:','["digestive system", "skeletal system", "nervous system", "integumentary system"]'::jsonb,2,'ANS regulates breathing.','original'),
('127.491.d.3.A',4,'Stimulating the sympathetic nervous system causes the bronchial airways to:','["shrink", "narrow", "close", "widen"]'::jsonb,3,'Sympathetic dilates airways.','original'),
('127.491.d.3.B',3,'The organs that help control acid-base balance by excreting hydrogen ions and conserving bicarbonate are the:','["kidneys", "lungs only", "liver only", "spleen"]'::jsonb,0,'Renal compensation.','original'),
('127.491.d.3.B',4,'Renal compensation for respiratory acidosis takes hours to days and works by retaining:','["carbon dioxide", "bicarbonate", "nitrogen", "oxygen"]'::jsonb,1,'Kidneys retain HCO3.','original'),
('127.491.d.3.C',3,'Heart failure can cause fluid to back up into the lungs, showing how the cardiac and respiratory systems:','["ignore each other", "never meet", "interact", "compete"]'::jsonb,2,'Systems interact.','original'),
('127.491.d.3.C',4,'A patient with a failing heart often has trouble breathing because blood backs up in the:','["skin", "bones", "digestive tract", "pulmonary circulation"]'::jsonb,3,'Congestion causes dyspnea.','original'),
('127.491.d.3.D',3,'On an EKG, a normal heartbeat pattern that starts in the sinus node at 60 to 100 beats per minute is called normal sinus:','["rhythm", "tumor", "failure", "breath"]'::jsonb,0,'NSR.','original'),
('127.491.d.3.D',4,'A chaotic, quivering rhythm of the ventricles that causes no effective pumping is ventricular:','["tachycardia sinus", "fibrillation", "standstill only", "bradycardia"]'::jsonb,1,'V-fib requires defibrillation.','original'),
('127.491.d.3.E',3,'A mechanical ventilator delivers breaths using pressure or:','["color", "music", "volume", "price"]'::jsonb,2,'Modes: volume or pressure.','original'),
('127.491.d.3.E',4,'The therapist adjusts the ventilator''s tidal volume, rate, and oxygen concentration based on the patient''s:','["insurance", "hobbies", "birthday", "blood gas results"]'::jsonb,3,'ABG-guided settings.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.A',3,'Slow, deep belly breathing taught to relax and improve ventilation is called:','["diaphragmatic breathing", "panting", "gasping", "sniffing"]'::jsonb,0,'Diaphragmatic breathing.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.A',4,'The incentive spirometer encourages a patient to take a slow, deep breath and hold it for at least:','["thirty seconds", "three seconds", "one second", "five minutes"]'::jsonb,1,'Hold 3-5 seconds.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.B',3,'In a lab simulation, the therapist uses a bag-valve-mask to provide breaths to a mannequin that is:','["sleeping", "laughing", "not breathing", "running"]'::jsonb,2,'BVM ventilation.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.B',4,'The head-tilt chin-lift maneuver helps open the airway by lifting the:','["feet", "stomach", "arms", "tongue away from the throat"]'::jsonb,3,'Tongue blocks the airway.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.C',3,'Using a device that vibrates the chest wall to help loosen mucus is an airway clearance:','["therapy", "menu", "report", "invoice"]'::jsonb,0,'Chest physiotherapy.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.C',4,'Patients with cystic fibrosis often use airway clearance because of thick:','["bones", "mucus", "hair", "blood"]'::jsonb,1,'CF produces thick secretions.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.D',3,'On a chest X-ray, air-filled normal lungs appear:','["white", "red", "dark", "green"]'::jsonb,2,'Air is dark.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.D',4,'Fluid or pneumonia in the lungs appears on a chest X-ray as a:','["hole", "clear area", "black area", "white area"]'::jsonb,3,'Infiltrates are white.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.E',3,'A normal arterial blood pH range is:','["7.35 to 7.45", "6.0 to 6.5", "1.0 to 2.0", "8.0 to 8.5"]'::jsonb,0,'Normal pH is slightly alkaline.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.E',4,'An ABG with pH 7.30 and PaCO2 55 mmHg suggests:','["normal values", "respiratory acidosis", "respiratory alkalosis", "metabolic alkalosis"]'::jsonb,1,'Low pH and high CO2.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.F',3,'A nasal cannula delivers a low oxygen flow, usually between 1 and 6:','["pounds per day", "cups per minute", "liters per minute", "inches per hour"]'::jsonb,2,'NC flow range.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.F',4,'For a patient who needs a high concentration of oxygen, the therapist may select a:','["room air", "nasal cannula at 1 L/min", "simple tape", "non-rebreather mask"]'::jsonb,3,'High FiO2.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.G',3,'Listening to breath sounds with a stethoscope is called:','["auscultation", "percussion", "palpation", "inspection"]'::jsonb,0,'Auscultation uses a stethoscope.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.G',4,'A high-pitched whistling sound heard on exhalation, common in asthma, is a:','["rub", "wheeze", "crackle", "snore"]'::jsonb,1,'Wheezes mean narrowed airways.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.H',3,'A care plan for a patient with asthma includes identifying triggers and using a controller medicine and a:','["crutch", "splint", "rescue inhaler", "blanket"]'::jsonb,2,'Asthma plan.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.H',4,'For COPD, a care plan encourages smoking cessation, vaccinations, and pulmonary:','["decoration", "tourism", "filing", "rehabilitation"]'::jsonb,3,'Pulmonary rehab.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.I',3,'In a simulated emergency, the respiratory therapist''s priority is to secure the patient''s:','["airway", "parking", "lunch", "paperwork"]'::jsonb,0,'Airway first.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.I',4,'In advanced life support, the therapist assists the team and monitors the patient''s oxygenation with:','["ruler", "capnography", "scale", "thermometer"]'::jsonb,1,'ETCO2 monitoring.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.J',3,'A therapist teaches a patient with COPD to recognize signs that the condition is getting worse, which is part of patient:','["billing", "parking", "education", "cooking"]'::jsonb,2,'Patient education.','original'),
('127.491.d.4.J',4,'Teaching a patient how to clean a nebulizer after each treatment helps prevent:','["boredom", "loud sounds", "fading", "infection"]'::jsonb,3,'Clean equipment.','original'),
('127.491.d.5.A',3,'Medications such as inhaled steroids and bronchodilators are applied in respiratory therapy to treat:','["airway inflammation and narrowing", "broken bones", "hair loss", "skin rashes"]'::jsonb,0,'Respiratory drugs treat airways.','original'),
('127.491.d.5.A',4,'A mucolytic agent is used in respiratory care to make mucus:','["darker", "thinner", "thicker", "sweeter"]'::jsonb,1,'Mucolytics thin mucus.','original'),
('127.491.d.5.B',3,'A patient with a known allergy to a medication should not receive it, since the allergy is a:','["side benefit", "indication", "contraindication", "dosage"]'::jsonb,2,'Contraindication.','original'),
('127.491.d.5.B',4,'Tremors and a fast heartbeat after albuterol are examples of a drug''s:','["orders", "labels", "indications", "side effects"]'::jsonb,3,'Side effects.','original'),
('127.491.d.5.C',3,'A dry powder inhaler requires the patient to breathe in:','["quickly and deeply", "through the nose only", "slowly and shallowly", "not at all"]'::jsonb,0,'DPI needs a strong inhale.','original'),
('127.491.d.5.C',4,'A small-volume nebulizer works best when the patient breathes:','["not at all", "slowly and deeply", "rapidly and shallowly", "only through the nose"]'::jsonb,1,'Slow deep breaths.','original'),
('127.491.d.5.D',3,'Before starting a bronchodilator treatment, the therapist records the patient''s heart rate, respiratory rate, and:','["shoe size", "address", "breath sounds", "insurance"]'::jsonb,2,'Baseline.','original'),
('127.491.d.5.D',4,'After a treatment, a decrease in wheezing and an improvement in peak flow suggest that the therapy was:','["wrong", "unnecessary", "harmful", "effective"]'::jsonb,3,'Response assessment.','original'),
('127.491.d.6.A',3,'A patient with capacity has the right to accept or refuse treatment, which is a part of informed:','["consent", "billing", "coding", "scheduling"]'::jsonb,0,'Informed consent.','original'),
('127.491.d.6.A',4,'The Patient''s Bill of Rights states that patients have the right to considerate and respectful:','["billing", "care", "gossip", "delays"]'::jsonb,1,'Rights.','original'),
('127.491.d.6.B',3,'Leaving a patient unattended on a ventilator without a handoff could be considered professional:','["training", "reward", "negligence", "recognition"]'::jsonb,2,'Negligence.','original'),
('127.491.d.6.B',4,'A therapist who is impaired by drugs or alcohol at work could lose their professional:','["lunch", "badge color", "parking", "license"]'::jsonb,3,'Impairment is unacceptable.','original'),
('127.491.d.6.C',3,'A document that states a patient''s wishes about being placed on a ventilator is an advance:','["directive", "receipt", "invoice", "agenda"]'::jsonb,0,'Advance directive.','original'),
('127.491.d.6.C',4,'A therapist may face an ethical dilemma when a family wants to continue ventilation but the patient previously stated a wish to:','["leave work", "stop treatment", "start treatment", "move rooms"]'::jsonb,1,'Dilemma: family versus patient wishes.','original'),
('127.491.d.7.A',3,'A respiratory therapist may advance professionally by earning a bachelor''s degree or specialty credentials such as the Adult Critical Care:','["Cleaner", "Cashier", "Specialist", "Chef"]'::jsonb,2,'ACCS credential.','original'),
('127.491.d.7.A',4,'A therapist who wants to become a department manager might pursue a degree in healthcare:','["art", "cooking", "fashion", "management"]'::jsonb,3,'Management path.','original'),
('127.491.d.7.B',3,'To work as a respiratory therapist in Texas, a graduate must pass the national exam and obtain a state:','["license", "discount", "parking pass", "coupon"]'::jsonb,0,'Licensure.','original'),
('127.491.d.7.B',4,'To keep a license active, therapists must complete a required number of continuing education:','["parties", "hours", "games", "songs"]'::jsonb,1,'CEUs.','original'),
('127.492.d.1.A',3,'Planning, organizing, and directing the operations of hospitals, clinics, and other health organizations is known as healthcare:','["sales", "design", "management", "tourism"]'::jsonb,2,'Healthcare management.','original')
