('127.492.d.3.B',3,'The law that protects the privacy of patient information is:','["ADA", "FDA", "HIPAA", "OSHA"]'::jsonb,2,'HIPAA.','original'),
('127.492.d.3.B',4,'The Patient''s Bill of Rights says patients have the right to know their treatment options and to give informed:','["feedback", "complaints only", "gifts", "consent"]'::jsonb,3,'Informed consent.','original'),
('127.492.d.3.C',3,'A manager who ignores repeated safety violations may be held legally responsible and face:','["fines or lawsuits", "praise", "promotions", "rewards"]'::jsonb,0,'Consequences.','original'),
('127.492.d.3.C',4,'Hiding a medical error from a patient is unethical and can lead to a loss of:','["weight", "trust", "paper", "luggage"]'::jsonb,1,'Honesty.','original'),
('127.492.d.3.D',3,'A hospital purchasing manager awards a contract to a company owned by a family member. This is a(n):','["fair practice", "budget plan", "conflict of interest", "safety check"]'::jsonb,2,'COI.','original'),
('127.492.d.3.D',4,'A conflict of interest should be disclosed to the organization so that decisions remain:','["rushed", "secret", "hidden", "unbiased"]'::jsonb,3,'Disclosure.','original'),
('127.492.d.3.E',3,'Billing for services never provided is fraud, while unnecessary use of resources is:','["waste", "profit", "income", "savings"]'::jsonb,0,'Fraud, waste, and abuse.','original'),
('127.492.d.3.E',4,'Actions that are not clearly intentional but are inconsistent with sound practices and cause unnecessary costs are called:','["audit", "abuse", "coding", "fraud"]'::jsonb,1,'Abuse vs fraud.','original'),
('127.493.d.1.A',3,'A nurse who holds a two-year degree and passes the NCLEX-PN exam is a licensed:','["dentist", "physician", "practical nurse", "nurse practitioner"]'::jsonb,2,'LPNs complete a practical nursing program.','original'),
('127.493.d.1.A',4,'Compared with an LPN, a registered nurse generally has a broader scope of practice and more:','["vacations", "pay stubs", "uniforms", "education"]'::jsonb,3,'RNs complete more schooling.','original'),
('127.493.d.1.B',3,'A student can become a registered nurse by earning an associate degree in nursing or a bachelor''s degree in nursing, abbreviated:','["BSN", "PhD", "JD", "MBA"]'::jsonb,0,'BSN.','original'),
('127.493.d.1.B',4,'After completing a nursing program, a graduate must pass the national licensing exam called the:','["ACT", "NCLEX-RN", "SAT", "GRE"]'::jsonb,1,'RN exam.','original'),
('127.493.d.1.C',3,'A nurse who has a master''s degree and provides primary care, diagnoses, and prescribes medicine is a nurse:','["aide", "orderly", "practitioner", "technician"]'::jsonb,2,'NPs are advanced practice.','original'),
('127.493.d.1.C',4,'A nurse anesthetist is an advanced practice nurse who specializes in giving:','["tours", "meals", "haircuts", "anesthesia"]'::jsonb,3,'CRNA.','original'),
('127.493.d.1.D',3,'A nurse who earns a PhD usually focuses on conducting:','["research", "cooking", "driving", "billing"]'::jsonb,0,'PhD = research.','original'),
('127.493.d.1.D',4,'The Doctor of Nursing Practice degree focuses mainly on advanced clinical practice and:','["art history", "leadership", "mathematics only", "poetry"]'::jsonb,1,'DNP.','original'),
('127.493.d.1.E',3,'A six-year career plan in nursing might start with an associate degree, followed by working as an RN, and then earning a:','["GED", "driver''s license", "BSN", "high school diploma"]'::jsonb,2,'Plan steps.','original'),
('127.493.d.1.E',4,'A good career plan lists short-term goals, long-term goals, and the steps needed to reach each, which are called:','["menus", "slogans", "rumors", "milestones"]'::jsonb,3,'Milestones.','original'),
('127.493.d.2.A',3,'The nursing hierarchy places a nurse manager above the staff nurse and the nurse aide, forming a chain of:','["command", "hobbies", "pay", "tests"]'::jsonb,0,'Hierarchy.','original'),
('127.493.d.2.A',4,'A chief nursing officer is at the top of the nursing hierarchy and reports to the hospital''s:','["patients", "executive leadership", "vendors", "visitors"]'::jsonb,1,'CNO.','original'),
('127.493.d.2.B',3,'A critical skill for a charge nurse who assigns patients to nurses is:','["cooking", "dancing", "delegation", "painting"]'::jsonb,2,'Delegation.','original'),
('127.493.d.2.B',4,'A competency expected of every nurse at all levels is the ability to follow safe, evidence-based:','["recipes", "routes", "dress codes", "practice"]'::jsonb,3,'Core competency.','original'),
('127.493.d.2.C',3,'Nurse aides provide basic care such as bathing and feeding, which supports the work of:','["registered nurses", "drivers", "chefs", "accountants"]'::jsonb,0,'Support roles.','original'),
('127.493.d.2.C',4,'When each level of the hierarchy performs its role well, patient:','["wait gets longer", "safety improves", "cost doubles", "care ends"]'::jsonb,1,'Impact of roles.','original'),
