('127.493.d.3.C',3,'A nurse who honors the principle of honesty with a patient is demonstrating professional:','["ethics", "fashion", "speed", "luck"]'::jsonb,0,'Ethics.','original'),
('127.493.d.3.C',4,'Respect for patient privacy is a professional value that is also required by the law called:','["ADA", "HIPAA", "OSHA", "FERPA"]'::jsonb,1,'HIPAA.','original'),
('127.493.d.3.D',3,'An experienced nurse who helps a new graduate learn the unit''s routines is acting as a:','["visitor", "patient", "mentor", "rival"]'::jsonb,2,'Mentoring.','original'),
('127.493.d.3.D',4,'A coaching plan for a new nurse should include goals, regular check-ins, and constructive:','["gossip", "punishment", "isolation", "feedback"]'::jsonb,3,'Coaching.','original'),
('127.493.d.3.E',3,'Handing a task to another team member while keeping responsibility for the outcome is:','["delegation", "abandonment", "avoidance", "competition"]'::jsonb,0,'Delegation.','original'),
('127.493.d.3.E',4,'When a nurse breaks a problem into steps, considers options, and chooses the best solution, the nurse is using:','["denial", "problem-solving", "guessing", "hesitation"]'::jsonb,1,'Decision-making process.','original'),
('127.493.d.4.A',3,'For a urgent change in a patient''s condition, the best communication method is typically a direct phone call or:','["an email next week", "a postcard", "face-to-face report", "a social media post"]'::jsonb,2,'Urgent matters need immediate contact.','original'),
('127.493.d.4.A',4,'A nurse should avoid sending patient names through unsecured text message because it could violate:','["parking rules", "traffic laws", "dress codes", "privacy rules"]'::jsonb,3,'Platform choice.','original'),
('127.493.d.4.B',3,'A tool used to communicate patient information between shifts in a structured way is the SBAR, which stands for Situation, Background, Assessment, and:','["Recommendation", "Rumor", "Reaction", "Record"]'::jsonb,0,'SBAR.','original'),
('127.493.d.4.B',4,'In writing a patient note, a nurse should be accurate, timely, and:','["emotional", "objective", "opinionated", "vague"]'::jsonb,1,'Charting.','original'),
('127.493.d.4.C',3,'For an emergent change such as a patient who stops breathing, the nurse should immediately call a:','["supply clerk", "billing office", "rapid response or code team", "parking attendant"]'::jsonb,2,'Emergency.','original'),
('127.493.d.4.C',4,'A routine question about a medication schedule is best handled through a non-urgent method like a message in the:','["overhead page", "emergency call", "shouted request", "electronic health record"]'::jsonb,3,'Routine matter.','original'),
('127.493.d.4.D',3,'When a supervisor offers feedback about a mistake, the best response is to listen and ask how to:','["improve", "hide", "argue", "ignore"]'::jsonb,0,'Receiving feedback.','original'),
('127.493.d.4.D',4,'When giving constructive criticism, a nurse should be specific, respectful, and focused on the:','["past mistakes", "behavior", "person''s family", "person''s appearance"]'::jsonb,1,'Giving feedback.','original'),
('127.493.d.5.A',3,'A daily agenda that lists tasks in order of importance helps a nurse to:','["forget", "relax", "prioritize", "procrastinate"]'::jsonb,2,'Prioritizing.','original'),
('127.493.d.5.A',4,'Using the ABCs of airway, breathing, and circulation helps a nurse decide which task to do:','["last", "later", "never", "first"]'::jsonb,3,'ABC priority.','original'),
('127.493.d.5.B',3,'A goal such as earning a certification within a year supports a nurse''s professional:','["growth", "delays", "rumors", "costs"]'::jsonb,0,'Professional goals.','original'),
('127.493.d.5.B',4,'A goal that is specific, measurable, achievable, relevant, and time-bound is called a:','["vague wish", "SMART goal", "rough idea", "random task"]'::jsonb,1,'SMART.','original'),
('127.493.d.5.C',3,'Interruptions, a cluttered workspace, and checking a phone often are factors that waste:','["food", "money", "time", "equipment"]'::jsonb,2,'Time wasters.','original'),
('127.493.d.5.C',4,'A strategy to improve time use is to group similar tasks together, such as giving all medications at one:','["day''s end", "patient request", "random moment", "scheduled round"]'::jsonb,3,'Batching.','original'),
('127.493.d.5.D',3,'Finishing a certification course in one year is a short-term goal, while becoming a nurse manager in ten years is a:','["long-term goal", "daily task", "vacation", "hobby"]'::jsonb,0,'Goal horizons.','original'),
('127.493.d.5.D',4,'To balance work and personal goals, a nurse can use a calendar to schedule work shifts, study time, and:','["delay", "rest", "gossip", "errors"]'::jsonb,1,'Balance.','original'),
('127.493.d.6.A',3,'An interdisciplinary team in a hospital might include a nurse, a physician, a social worker, and a:','["architect", "accountant", "physical therapist", "tourist"]'::jsonb,2,'Interdisciplinary.','original'),
('127.493.d.6.A',4,'The purpose of an interdisciplinary team is to coordinate care so that the patient''s needs are met by the combined skills of:','["no one", "the patient only", "one profession", "several professions"]'::jsonb,3,'Collaborative care.','original'),
('127.493.d.6.B',3,'Activities done to help team members get to know each other and work together better are called team-:','["building exercises", "dividing games", "ending rules", "breaking tasks"]'::jsonb,0,'Team building.','original'),
('127.493.d.6.B',4,'A plan for creating a strong team should include clear roles, shared goals, and open:','["secrets", "communication", "silence", "rivalry"]'::jsonb,1,'Team plan.','original'),
('127.493.d.6.C',3,'Two nurses disagree about the best way to handle a task. A positive way to manage the conflict is to listen to each other and focus on the:','["past", "person", "problem", "blame"]'::jsonb,2,'Conflict management.','original'),
('127.493.d.6.C',4,'When a conflict cannot be solved between two coworkers, they can ask a neutral third party, such as a supervisor, to help with:','["gossip", "punishment", "competition", "mediation"]'::jsonb,3,'Mediation.','original'),
('127.493.d.6.D',3,'Tuckman''s stages of team development are forming, storming, norming, and:','["performing", "hiding", "sleeping", "quitting"]'::jsonb,0,'Tuckman.','original'),
('127.493.d.6.D',4,'The stage when team members disagree and compete for roles is called:','["norming", "storming", "forming", "adjourning"]'::jsonb,1,'Storming.','original'),
('127.493.d.7.A',3,'The state agency that licenses nurses and enforces the practice act for the profession is the Board of:','["Commerce", "Education", "Nursing", "Health Fitness"]'::jsonb,2,'BON.','original'),
('127.493.d.7.A',4,'The Board of Nursing can discipline a nurse who violates the Nursing Practice Act by suspending or revoking the nurse''s:','["uniform", "lunch break", "parking permit", "license"]'::jsonb,3,'Discipline.','original'),
('127.493.d.7.B',3,'A local health department is an example of a(n):','["public health agency", "sports team", "private store", "bank"]'::jsonb,0,'Agencies.','original'),
('127.493.d.7.B',4,'The federal agency that enforces workplace safety rules for nurses, such as protection from needlesticks, is:','["DEA", "OSHA", "CDC", "FDA"]'::jsonb,1,'OSHA.','original'),
('127.493.d.7.C',3,'The tasks and actions that a nurse is legally allowed to perform based on education and licensure are the nursing scope of:','["rest", "display", "practice", "luck"]'::jsonb,2,'Scope.','original'),
('127.493.d.7.C',4,'A nurse who is asked to do a task outside their scope of practice should:','["do it anyway", "ignore the request silently", "guess", "decline and tell the supervisor"]'::jsonb,3,'Stay within scope.','original'),
('127.493.d.7.D',3,'A document that shows a nurse has met the legal requirements to practice is a:','["license", "résumé", "badge", "certificate of attendance"]'::jsonb,0,'Licensure is legal.','original'),
('127.493.d.7.D',4,'A voluntary credential that shows expertise in a specialty, such as critical care, is a:','["license", "certification", "diploma", "permit"]'::jsonb,1,'Certification is voluntary.','original'),
('127.493.d.7.E',3,'The Board of Nursing regulates practice to protect the public, while a professional nursing organization mainly promotes the:','["price of drugs", "building codes", "interests of nurses", "interests of the government"]'::jsonb,2,'Roles differ.','original'),
('127.493.d.7.E',4,'Joining a professional nursing organization such as the American Nurses Association provides networking and:','["parking", "coupons", "uniforms", "continuing education"]'::jsonb,3,'Organization benefits.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
